                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Chapter 4 combines data from the 2016 and 2019 FinAccess surveys of Kenya. The FinAccess surveys are repeated cross-section surveys that provide demand-side information on the use of financial services among the adult population in Kenya. The surveys are conducted using a unique household sampling frame based on the 5th National Sample Survey and Evaluation Programme designed to yield a nationally representative sample."
                },
